The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/pv-sizing/pvsize-07-roof-shape-inference.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

| Severity | Count | Key Issues |
|----------|-------|------------|
| **High** | 2 | Gable default fallback is anti-conservative (2.14× overestimation for misclassified hips); no user override mechanism exists |
| **Medium** | 3 | Tile/slate material as deterministic Hip predictor is unreliable; fragile string matching for apartment→Flat; latitude <30° heuristic has no empirical basis |
| **Low** | 2 | Missing test coverage for 2-plane hip edge cases; no vendor reference implementation for roof shape classification |

**Core concern**: The inference ruleset is ordered such that ambiguous evidence defaults to Gable (0.75), the most permissive shape, while Hip (0.35) is the correct conservative default. A hip roof with only 2 recorded planes (common HPXML limitation) receives a PV capacity estimate 2.14× too high, with no mechanism for users to correct it.
